NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"sqlite-temporal-persistence-reproduction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SQLite Temporal persistence reproduction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Issue: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/issues/2034","children":[{"type":"text","value":"#2034"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nOwner: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db-sqlite-persistence-core/tests/sqlite-temporal-value-oracle.test.ts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SQLite typed-value oracle"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"revision-and-scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revision and scope"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recorded 2026-10-05 against production commit\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"84dc899bfc8d6a16487c1584dbb1cb177109aacc"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":").\nBranch: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codex/temporal-persistence-oracle"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe oracle is an uncommitted diagnostic addition with SHA-256\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ec38aeca3145a6b51561247d3dc3996ab50a05317414d070147728130ffd656b"},{"type":"text","value":".\nProduction code is unchanged. This is a reproduction, not a bug-class repair."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The requested Temporal preservation behavior comes from the issue. Existing\ncore tests establish Date/BigInt preservation but do not establish a complete\nTemporal support policy. Explicit rejection remains an alternative product\nchoice. These tests deliberately expect preservation and remain RED; they are\nnot expected-failure tests and must not be presented as passing CI."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The independent model assigns two fixture ordinals to earlier/later values.\nIt predicts literal type/text observations and query keys without production\nserialization, comparison, or SQL helpers. It does not prescribe stored bytes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"execution-receipt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution receipt"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime: macOS arm64, Node 24.19.0, SQLite 3.53.3, Vitest 3.2.4,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temporal-polyfill"},{"type":"text","value":" 0.3.0. The issue used polyfill 0.3.2; this reproduction uses\nthe repository's existing locked version."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full bounded matrix ran 21 tests: "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"13 passed, 8 failed"}]},{"type":"text","value":", exit 1.\nAll 16 production cases reached a file-backed SQLite close/reopen.\nEight Date/ISO-string control cases and five checker-calibration tests passed.\nAll eight Instant/PlainDate cases failed at public value checkpoints."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observation after reopen"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporal result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadSubset"},{"type":"text","value":" hydration and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scanRows"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct and nested values restored as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":"; inline and separate row metadata also lost their type and value."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadCollectionMetadata"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct and nested values restored as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pullSince"},{"type":"text","value":" from the previous committed position"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row values, separate row metadata, and collection metadata in the replay payload restored as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equality at the earlier value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of the earlier row's key."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Greater-than the earlier value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of the later row's key."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ascending one-row windows, offsets 0 and 1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Insert order happens to match; after the values swap, both pages retain the old order and fail."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both index configurations produce these results. Indexed cases verify that\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ensureIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" installed a real SQLite index and that it survives reopen. They\ndo not assert optimizer index use. The existing expression-index owner retains\nthat responsibility. Query failures on corrupted values do not independently\nestablish a compiler defect with correctly encoded Temporal values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The selected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PlainDate / update / indexed=false"},{"type":"text","value":" replay ran one test, skipped\n20, and failed all eight named checkpoints (exit 1). Its hydration diff includes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"expected stamp: { kind: \"PlainDate\", text: \"2026-01-02\" }\nactual stamp:   {}\nexpected equality keys: [\"a-late\"]\nactual equality keys:   []\nexpected first page:    [\"a-late\"]\nactual first page:      [\"z-early\"]","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The normal package configuration includes this new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" file. With a\ncomplete dependency installation, its standard focused command is:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm --filter @tanstack/db-sqlite-persistence-core test \\\n  tests/sqlite-temporal-value-oracle.test.ts \\\n  --coverage.enabled=false --typecheck.enabled=false","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fresh installation could not complete: the configured package proxy returned\n403 for Rollup 4.64.0, and the public registry returned 503. The stalled retry\nwas stopped. The standard command above was therefore not the local receipt.\nLocal execution used cached test tools, a temporary Vite configuration, and\nexplicit aliases to "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"this worktree's"}]},{"type":"text","value":" DB, db-ivm, and persistence source.\nExternal libraries came from the existing checkout. No prebuilt DB distribution\nor mocked persistence adapter supplied the result."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exact local commands:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/Users/kyle.mathews/programs/tanstack-db/node_modules/.bin/vitest run \\\n  --config /private/tmp/temporal-persistence-vitest.config.mjs \\\n  --reporter=json --outputFile=/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-final.json\n\n/Users/kyle.mathews/programs/tanstack-db/node_modules/.bin/vitest run \\\n  --config /private/tmp/temporal-persistence-vitest.config.mjs \\\n  -t 'PlainDate.*update.*indexed=false'","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The JSON report and selected replay log are local scratch receipts at\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-final.json"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-replay.log"},{"type":"text","value":". The results above preserve the\nverdict-critical evidence without depending on those temporary files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript checking of the oracle and its imported source passed (exit 0), using\na temporary config with source and cached dependency aliases. ESLint passed\nwithout warnings (exit 0); Prettier formatting passed. A full package test run\nand a full frozen-lockfile installation are not claimed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-previous-tests-missed-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why previous tests missed it"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared core adapter's typed-value test supplies Date and BigInt. The Node\nexpression-index grammar supplies scalar values, Date, and BigInt. Neither\nsupplies real Temporal objects or observes their type plus text across reopen.\nMore runs over those domains cannot reach the issue."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The new owner adds that missing value domain and explicit native-type\nobservation. Its file-handle lifecycle is separate from the shared contract's\ninjected harness because an adapter recreation alone does not prove physical\nSQLite close/reopen. Existing tests and expectations are preserved."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"oracle-guide-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Oracle guide evidence"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-001 authority and limits"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Established Date controls; requested Temporal extension explicitly identified as diagnostic, with support/rejection policy unresolved."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-002 independent judgment"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Literal type/text model and ordinal-based key expectations; no production semantic helpers."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-003 responsibilities"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Opening law/limits, expected-value and expected-row model, 16-cell grammar, real SQLite driver, and named public comparisons are in the oracle."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-004 grammar controls"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Four kinds × insert/update × absent/present index; unique-cell/count calibration. Each axis's contribution is stated in the header. Two adjacent ISO days bound the range. Unique keys and increasing positions exclude duplicate inserts and stale transaction positions."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-005 production reach"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each test commits through the real adapter, replaces the SQLite handle and adapter, verifies index presence/absence, and checks hydration, scan, metadata, replay, and query results."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-006 calibration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Five passing checks reject empty-object loss, ISO-string type erasure, same-kind wrong values, omissions, duplicates, and reversed output through the same checker. Unmodified production itself fails at the intended checkpoints; no production mutant was installed."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-007 campaigns/replay"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Random-campaign requirement does not apply to bounded enumeration. All 16 cells execute. Selected-name replay was checked and reproduces the same mismatch."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-008 state minimality"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No state machine added. A pure recomputation retains kind, value ordinal, key, and insert/update history because each changes a checked output."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-009 vocabulary"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses adapter transaction, row metadata, collection metadata, replay, and checkpoint terms. Type/text records are explicitly model-only observations."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-010 failure fidelity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Soft assertions retain all reached mismatches before teardown; Vitest separately reports afterEach failures. Registered harness cleanup closes the handle and removes its owned temporary directory. No shrinking."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-011 second formulation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No shared semantic comparator is used: the query model uses fixture ordinals. No separate formulation is claimed or needed to identify this serialization loss."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-012 review evidence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This record names the production revision, oracle hash, outcomes, execution limitations, and open scope. No closure claim."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-013 distinguishing boundary"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same-type distinct dates, equality versus strictly greater, swapped values, both page offsets, and index presence distinguish empty-object/type-erasure designs within the finite grammar. No arbitrary-value or threshold proof."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-014 host handoff"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SQLite itself stores the file and supplies reopen results; Temporal comes from a real polyfill. The thin sequential driver does not claim production Node-driver, Expo, OPFS, or native mobile conformance."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"open-scope-and-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open scope and ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Issue #2034 and this typed-value owner retain the support/rejection decision,\nother Temporal kinds, native constructors, precision/calendar variations,\ntruncate/delete and longer histories, compatibility with old bytes, and host\nreceiving witnesses. A future support repair must cover literal encoding and\nindex/comparison behavior in the expression-index owner as well. The current\nreachable counterexamples keep the bug class open."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"current-main-replay-and-design-follow-up","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current-main replay and design follow-up"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On 2026-10-05 the worktree was fast-forwarded without conflicts to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"e21c280f3c4e56f6c0d05ec0eed87db29c623489"},{"type":"text","value":", including #2002. The unmodified\nTemporal oracle again ran 21 tests: 13 passed, 8 failed, exit 1, using the same\ncached-tool/source-alias setup. Its captured report is\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-current-main.json"},{"type":"text","value":". This extends the RED\nreceipt; it does not supersede the original revision record above."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The exploratory "},{"type":"link","href":"issue-2034-design/README.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"design grammar and stress readings"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nmap the proposed value-domain repair to current primary oracle owners. They do\nnot implement a fix, revise established lifecycle laws, or claim closure."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"implemented-v2-follow-up-2026-10-05","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implemented v2 follow-up — 2026-10-05"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"issue-2034-design/v2.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2 design grammar"}]},{"type":"text","value":" now specifies and implements\nnative Instant/PlainDate preservation, shared SQL/index representations and\nremote-demand admission limits. Existing owners were extended before the repair;\noriginal-production and hostile controls demonstrate distinguishing failures.\nThe final affected suite has 471 passing tests, one existing TODO and no failures;\nTypeScript and lint pass (25 existing lint warnings). The linked evidence keeps\nexact source hashes, receiving limits and separate production/test/doc weight.\nThis supersedes the open implementation status above while preserving its RED\nreceipts. It does not establish native multiprocess or untested host support."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"sqlite-temporal-persistence-reproduction","text":"SQLite Temporal persistence reproduction","level":1},{"id":"revision-and-scope","text":"Revision and scope","level":2},{"id":"execution-receipt","text":"Execution receipt","level":2},{"id":"why-previous-tests-missed-it","text":"Why previous tests missed it","level":2},{"id":"oracle-guide-evidence","text":"Oracle guide evidence","level":2},{"id":"open-scope-and-ownership","text":"Open scope and ownership","level":2},{"id":"current-main-replay-and-design-follow-up","text":"Current-main replay and design follow-up","level":2},{"id":"implemented-v2-follow-up-2026-10-05","text":"Implemented v2 follow-up — 2026-10-05","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# SQLite Temporal persistence reproduction\n\nIssue: [#2034](https://github.com/TanStack/db/issues/2034).\nOwner: [SQLite typed-value oracle](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db-sqlite-persistence-core/tests/sqlite-temporal-value-oracle.test.ts).\n\n## Revision and scope\n\nRecorded 2026-10-05 against production commit\n`84dc899bfc8d6a16487c1584dbb1cb177109aacc` (`origin/main`).\nBranch: `codex/temporal-persistence-oracle`.\nThe oracle is an uncommitted diagnostic addition with SHA-256\n`ec38aeca3145a6b51561247d3dc3996ab50a05317414d070147728130ffd656b`.\nProduction code is unchanged. This is a reproduction, not a bug-class repair.\n\nThe requested Temporal preservation behavior comes from the issue. Existing\ncore tests establish Date/BigInt preservation but do not establish a complete\nTemporal support policy. Explicit rejection remains an alternative product\nchoice. These tests deliberately expect preservation and remain RED; they are\nnot expected-failure tests and must not be presented as passing CI.\n\nThe independent model assigns two fixture ordinals to earlier/later values.\nIt predicts literal type/text observations and query keys without production\nserialization, comparison, or SQL helpers. It does not prescribe stored bytes.\n\n## Execution receipt\n\nRuntime: macOS arm64, Node 24.19.0, SQLite 3.53.3, Vitest 3.2.4,\n`temporal-polyfill` 0.3.0. The issue used polyfill 0.3.2; this reproduction uses\nthe repository's existing locked version.\n\nThe full bounded matrix ran 21 tests: **13 passed, 8 failed**, exit 1.\nAll 16 production cases reached a file-backed SQLite close/reopen.\nEight Date/ISO-string control cases and five checker-calibration tests passed.\nAll eight Instant/PlainDate cases failed at public value checkpoints.\n\n| Observation after reopen | Temporal result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `loadSubset` hydration and `scanRows` | Direct and nested values restored as `{}`; inline and separate row metadata also lost their type and value. |\n| `loadCollectionMetadata` | Direct and nested values restored as `{}`. |\n| `pullSince` from the previous committed position | Row values, separate row metadata, and collection metadata in the replay payload restored as `{}`. |\n| Equality at the earlier value | `[]` instead of the earlier row's key. |\n| Greater-than the earlier value | `[]` instead of the later row's key. |\n| Ascending one-row windows, offsets 0 and 1 | Insert order happens to match; after the values swap, both pages retain the old order and fail. |\n\nBoth index configurations produce these results. Indexed cases verify that\n`ensureIndex` installed a real SQLite index and that it survives reopen. They\ndo not assert optimizer index use. The existing expression-index owner retains\nthat responsibility. Query failures on corrupted values do not independently\nestablish a compiler defect with correctly encoded Temporal values.\n\nThe selected `PlainDate / update / indexed=false` replay ran one test, skipped\n20, and failed all eight named checkpoints (exit 1). Its hydration diff includes:\n\n```text\nexpected stamp: { kind: \"PlainDate\", text: \"2026-01-02\" }\nactual stamp:   {}\nexpected equality keys: [\"a-late\"]\nactual equality keys:   []\nexpected first page:    [\"a-late\"]\nactual first page:      [\"z-early\"]\n```\n\nThe normal package configuration includes this new `*.test.ts` file. With a\ncomplete dependency installation, its standard focused command is:\n\n```sh\npnpm --filter @tanstack/db-sqlite-persistence-core test \\\n  tests/sqlite-temporal-value-oracle.test.ts \\\n  --coverage.enabled=false --typecheck.enabled=false\n```\n\nThe fresh installation could not complete: the configured package proxy returned\n403 for Rollup 4.64.0, and the public registry returned 503. The stalled retry\nwas stopped. The standard command above was therefore not the local receipt.\nLocal execution used cached test tools, a temporary Vite configuration, and\nexplicit aliases to **this worktree's** DB, db-ivm, and persistence source.\nExternal libraries came from the existing checkout. No prebuilt DB distribution\nor mocked persistence adapter supplied the result.\n\nExact local commands:\n\n```sh\n/Users/kyle.mathews/programs/tanstack-db/node_modules/.bin/vitest run \\\n  --config /private/tmp/temporal-persistence-vitest.config.mjs \\\n  --reporter=json --outputFile=/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-final.json\n\n/Users/kyle.mathews/programs/tanstack-db/node_modules/.bin/vitest run \\\n  --config /private/tmp/temporal-persistence-vitest.config.mjs \\\n  -t 'PlainDate.*update.*indexed=false'\n```\n\nThe JSON report and selected replay log are local scratch receipts at\n`/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-final.json` and\n`/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-replay.log`. The results above preserve the\nverdict-critical evidence without depending on those temporary files.\n\nTypeScript checking of the oracle and its imported source passed (exit 0), using\na temporary config with source and cached dependency aliases. ESLint passed\nwithout warnings (exit 0); Prettier formatting passed. A full package test run\nand a full frozen-lockfile installation are not claimed.\n\n## Why previous tests missed it\n\nThe shared core adapter's typed-value test supplies Date and BigInt. The Node\nexpression-index grammar supplies scalar values, Date, and BigInt. Neither\nsupplies real Temporal objects or observes their type plus text across reopen.\nMore runs over those domains cannot reach the issue.\n\nThe new owner adds that missing value domain and explicit native-type\nobservation. Its file-handle lifecycle is separate from the shared contract's\ninjected harness because an adapter recreation alone does not prove physical\nSQLite close/reopen. Existing tests and expectations are preserved.\n\n## Oracle guide evidence\n\n| Requirement | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 authority and limits | Established Date controls; requested Temporal extension explicitly identified as diagnostic, with support/rejection policy unresolved. |\n| ORC-002 independent judgment | Literal type/text model and ordinal-based key expectations; no production semantic helpers. |\n| ORC-003 responsibilities | Opening law/limits, expected-value and expected-row model, 16-cell grammar, real SQLite driver, and named public comparisons are in the oracle. |\n| ORC-004 grammar controls | Four kinds × insert/update × absent/present index; unique-cell/count calibration. Each axis's contribution is stated in the header. Two adjacent ISO days bound the range. Unique keys and increasing positions exclude duplicate inserts and stale transaction positions. |\n| ORC-005 production reach | Each test commits through the real adapter, replaces the SQLite handle and adapter, verifies index presence/absence, and checks hydration, scan, metadata, replay, and query results. |\n| ORC-006 calibration | Five passing checks reject empty-object loss, ISO-string type erasure, same-kind wrong values, omissions, duplicates, and reversed output through the same checker. Unmodified production itself fails at the intended checkpoints; no production mutant was installed. |\n| ORC-007 campaigns/replay | Random-campaign requirement does not apply to bounded enumeration. All 16 cells execute. Selected-name replay was checked and reproduces the same mismatch. |\n| ORC-008 state minimality | No state machine added. A pure recomputation retains kind, value ordinal, key, and insert/update history because each changes a checked output. |\n| ORC-009 vocabulary | Uses adapter transaction, row metadata, collection metadata, replay, and checkpoint terms. Type/text records are explicitly model-only observations. |\n| ORC-010 failure fidelity | Soft assertions retain all reached mismatches before teardown; Vitest separately reports afterEach failures. Registered harness cleanup closes the handle and removes its owned temporary directory. No shrinking. |\n| ORC-011 second formulation | No shared semantic comparator is used: the query model uses fixture ordinals. No separate formulation is claimed or needed to identify this serialization loss. |\n| ORC-012 review evidence | This record names the production revision, oracle hash, outcomes, execution limitations, and open scope. No closure claim. |\n| ORC-013 distinguishing boundary | Same-type distinct dates, equality versus strictly greater, swapped values, both page offsets, and index presence distinguish empty-object/type-erasure designs within the finite grammar. No arbitrary-value or threshold proof. |\n| ORC-014 host handoff | SQLite itself stores the file and supplies reopen results; Temporal comes from a real polyfill. The thin sequential driver does not claim production Node-driver, Expo, OPFS, or native mobile conformance. |\n\n## Open scope and ownership\n\nIssue #2034 and this typed-value owner retain the support/rejection decision,\nother Temporal kinds, native constructors, precision/calendar variations,\ntruncate/delete and longer histories, compatibility with old bytes, and host\nreceiving witnesses. A future support repair must cover literal encoding and\nindex/comparison behavior in the expression-index owner as well. The current\nreachable counterexamples keep the bug class open.\n\n\n## Current-main replay and design follow-up\n\nOn 2026-10-05 the worktree was fast-forwarded without conflicts to\n`e21c280f3c4e56f6c0d05ec0eed87db29c623489`, including #2002. The unmodified\nTemporal oracle again ran 21 tests: 13 passed, 8 failed, exit 1, using the same\ncached-tool/source-alias setup. Its captured report is\n`/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-current-main.json`. This extends the RED\nreceipt; it does not supersede the original revision record above.\n\nThe exploratory [design grammar and stress readings](issue-2034-design/README.md)\nmap the proposed value-domain repair to current primary oracle owners. They do\nnot implement a fix, revise established lifecycle laws, or claim closure.\n\n\n## Implemented v2 follow-up — 2026-10-05\n\nThe [v2 design grammar](issue-2034-design/v2.md) now specifies and implements\nnative Instant/PlainDate preservation, shared SQL/index representations and\nremote-demand admission limits. Existing owners were extended before the repair;\noriginal-production and hostile controls demonstrate distinguishing failures.\nThe final affected suite has 471 passing tests, one existing TODO and no failures;\nTypeScript and lint pass (25 existing lint warnings). The linked evidence keeps\nexact source hashes, receiving limits and separate production/test/doc weight.\nThis supersedes the open implementation status above while preserving its RED\nreceipts. It does not establish native multiprocess or untested host support.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# SQLite Temporal persistence reproduction\n\nIssue: [#2034](https://github.com/TanStack/db/issues/2034).\nOwner: [SQLite typed-value oracle](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db-sqlite-persistence-core/tests/sqlite-temporal-value-oracle.test.ts).\n\n## Revision and scope\n\nRecorded 2026-10-05 against production commit\n`84dc899bfc8d6a16487c1584dbb1cb177109aacc` (`origin/main`).\nBranch: `codex/temporal-persistence-oracle`.\nThe oracle is an uncommitted diagnostic addition with SHA-256\n`ec38aeca3145a6b51561247d3dc3996ab50a05317414d070147728130ffd656b`.\nProduction code is unchanged. This is a reproduction, not a bug-class repair.\n\nThe requested Temporal preservation behavior comes from the issue. Existing\ncore tests establish Date/BigInt preservation but do not establish a complete\nTemporal support policy. Explicit rejection remains an alternative product\nchoice. These tests deliberately expect preservation and remain RED; they are\nnot expected-failure tests and must not be presented as passing CI.\n\nThe independent model assigns two fixture ordinals to earlier/later values.\nIt predicts literal type/text observations and query keys without production\nserialization, comparison, or SQL helpers. It does not prescribe stored bytes.\n\n## Execution receipt\n\nRuntime: macOS arm64, Node 24.19.0, SQLite 3.53.3, Vitest 3.2.4,\n`temporal-polyfill` 0.3.0. The issue used polyfill 0.3.2; this reproduction uses\nthe repository's existing locked version.\n\nThe full bounded matrix ran 21 tests: **13 passed, 8 failed**, exit 1.\nAll 16 production cases reached a file-backed SQLite close/reopen.\nEight Date/ISO-string control cases and five checker-calibration tests passed.\nAll eight Instant/PlainDate cases failed at public value checkpoints.\n\n| Observation after reopen | Temporal result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `loadSubset` hydration and `scanRows` | Direct and nested values restored as `{}`; inline and separate row metadata also lost their type and value. |\n| `loadCollectionMetadata` | Direct and nested values restored as `{}`. |\n| `pullSince` from the previous committed position | Row values, separate row metadata, and collection metadata in the replay payload restored as `{}`. |\n| Equality at the earlier value | `[]` instead of the earlier row's key. |\n| Greater-than the earlier value | `[]` instead of the later row's key. |\n| Ascending one-row windows, offsets 0 and 1 | Insert order happens to match; after the values swap, both pages retain the old order and fail. |\n\nBoth index configurations produce these results. Indexed cases verify that\n`ensureIndex` installed a real SQLite index and that it survives reopen. They\ndo not assert optimizer index use. The existing expression-index owner retains\nthat responsibility. Query failures on corrupted values do not independently\nestablish a compiler defect with correctly encoded Temporal values.\n\nThe selected `PlainDate / update / indexed=false` replay ran one test, skipped\n20, and failed all eight named checkpoints (exit 1). Its hydration diff includes:\n\n```text\nexpected stamp: { kind: \"PlainDate\", text: \"2026-01-02\" }\nactual stamp:   {}\nexpected equality keys: [\"a-late\"]\nactual equality keys:   []\nexpected first page:    [\"a-late\"]\nactual first page:      [\"z-early\"]\n```\n\nThe normal package configuration includes this new `*.test.ts` file. With a\ncomplete dependency installation, its standard focused command is:\n\n```sh\npnpm --filter @tanstack/db-sqlite-persistence-core test \\\n  tests/sqlite-temporal-value-oracle.test.ts \\\n  --coverage.enabled=false --typecheck.enabled=false\n```\n\nThe fresh installation could not complete: the configured package proxy returned\n403 for Rollup 4.64.0, and the public registry returned 503. The stalled retry\nwas stopped. The standard command above was therefore not the local receipt.\nLocal execution used cached test tools, a temporary Vite configuration, and\nexplicit aliases to **this worktree's** DB, db-ivm, and persistence source.\nExternal libraries came from the existing checkout. No prebuilt DB distribution\nor mocked persistence adapter supplied the result.\n\nExact local commands:\n\n```sh\n/Users/kyle.mathews/programs/tanstack-db/node_modules/.bin/vitest run \\\n  --config /private/tmp/temporal-persistence-vitest.config.mjs \\\n  --reporter=json --outputFile=/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-final.json\n\n/Users/kyle.mathews/programs/tanstack-db/node_modules/.bin/vitest run \\\n  --config /private/tmp/temporal-persistence-vitest.config.mjs \\\n  -t 'PlainDate.*update.*indexed=false'\n```\n\nThe JSON report and selected replay log are local scratch receipts at\n`/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-final.json` and\n`/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-replay.log`. The results above preserve the\nverdict-critical evidence without depending on those temporary files.\n\nTypeScript checking of the oracle and its imported source passed (exit 0), using\na temporary config with source and cached dependency aliases. ESLint passed\nwithout warnings (exit 0); Prettier formatting passed. A full package test run\nand a full frozen-lockfile installation are not claimed.\n\n## Why previous tests missed it\n\nThe shared core adapter's typed-value test supplies Date and BigInt. The Node\nexpression-index grammar supplies scalar values, Date, and BigInt. Neither\nsupplies real Temporal objects or observes their type plus text across reopen.\nMore runs over those domains cannot reach the issue.\n\nThe new owner adds that missing value domain and explicit native-type\nobservation. Its file-handle lifecycle is separate from the shared contract's\ninjected harness because an adapter recreation alone does not prove physical\nSQLite close/reopen. Existing tests and expectations are preserved.\n\n## Oracle guide evidence\n\n| Requirement | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 authority and limits | Established Date controls; requested Temporal extension explicitly identified as diagnostic, with support/rejection policy unresolved. |\n| ORC-002 independent judgment | Literal type/text model and ordinal-based key expectations; no production semantic helpers. |\n| ORC-003 responsibilities | Opening law/limits, expected-value and expected-row model, 16-cell grammar, real SQLite driver, and named public comparisons are in the oracle. |\n| ORC-004 grammar controls | Four kinds × insert/update × absent/present index; unique-cell/count calibration. Each axis's contribution is stated in the header. Two adjacent ISO days bound the range. Unique keys and increasing positions exclude duplicate inserts and stale transaction positions. |\n| ORC-005 production reach | Each test commits through the real adapter, replaces the SQLite handle and adapter, verifies index presence/absence, and checks hydration, scan, metadata, replay, and query results. |\n| ORC-006 calibration | Five passing checks reject empty-object loss, ISO-string type erasure, same-kind wrong values, omissions, duplicates, and reversed output through the same checker. Unmodified production itself fails at the intended checkpoints; no production mutant was installed. |\n| ORC-007 campaigns/replay | Random-campaign requirement does not apply to bounded enumeration. All 16 cells execute. Selected-name replay was checked and reproduces the same mismatch. |\n| ORC-008 state minimality | No state machine added. A pure recomputation retains kind, value ordinal, key, and insert/update history because each changes a checked output. |\n| ORC-009 vocabulary | Uses adapter transaction, row metadata, collection metadata, replay, and checkpoint terms. Type/text records are explicitly model-only observations. |\n| ORC-010 failure fidelity | Soft assertions retain all reached mismatches before teardown; Vitest separately reports afterEach failures. Registered harness cleanup closes the handle and removes its owned temporary directory. No shrinking. |\n| ORC-011 second formulation | No shared semantic comparator is used: the query model uses fixture ordinals. No separate formulation is claimed or needed to identify this serialization loss. |\n| ORC-012 review evidence | This record names the production revision, oracle hash, outcomes, execution limitations, and open scope. No closure claim. |\n| ORC-013 distinguishing boundary | Same-type distinct dates, equality versus strictly greater, swapped values, both page offsets, and index presence distinguish empty-object/type-erasure designs within the finite grammar. No arbitrary-value or threshold proof. |\n| ORC-014 host handoff | SQLite itself stores the file and supplies reopen results; Temporal comes from a real polyfill. The thin sequential driver does not claim production Node-driver, Expo, OPFS, or native mobile conformance. |\n\n## Open scope and ownership\n\nIssue #2034 and this typed-value owner retain the support/rejection decision,\nother Temporal kinds, native constructors, precision/calendar variations,\ntruncate/delete and longer histories, compatibility with old bytes, and host\nreceiving witnesses. A future support repair must cover literal encoding and\nindex/comparison behavior in the expression-index owner as well. The current\nreachable counterexamples keep the bug class open.\n\n\n## Current-main replay and design follow-up\n\nOn 2026-10-05 the worktree was fast-forwarded without conflicts to\n`e21c280f3c4e56f6c0d05ec0eed87db29c623489`, including #2002. The unmodified\nTemporal oracle again ran 21 tests: 13 passed, 8 failed, exit 1, using the same\ncached-tool/source-alias setup. Its captured report is\n`/private/tmp/temporal-persistence-current-main.json`. This extends the RED\nreceipt; it does not supersede the original revision record above.\n\nThe exploratory [design grammar and stress readings](issue-2034-design/README.md)\nmap the proposed value-domain repair to current primary oracle owners. They do\nnot implement a fix, revise established lifecycle laws, or claim closure.\n\n\n## Implemented v2 follow-up — 2026-10-05\n\nThe [v2 design grammar](issue-2034-design/v2.md) now specifies and implements\nnative Instant/PlainDate preservation, shared SQL/index representations and\nremote-demand admission limits. Existing owners were extended before the repair;\noriginal-production and hostile controls demonstrate distinguishing failures.\nThe final affected suite has 471 passing tests, one existing TODO and no failures;\nTypeScript and lint pass (25 existing lint warnings). The linked evidence keeps\nexact source hashes, receiving limits and separate production/test/doc weight.\nThis supersedes the open implementation status above while preserving its RED\nreceipts. It does not establish native multiprocess or untested host support.\n"}
